This independent Pi extension includes adapted guidance and protocol designs
from OpenAI Codex, pinned to rust-v0.114.0, commit
b9904c0ae4ecb773549efd6ea3fb05229402fdb9, under Apache License 2.0.
The Pi integration, scheduler, controlled process execution, question queue,
tracked mutation layer, JSON-RPC LSP client and UI use JavaScript and Pi APIs.
The core guidance is condensed and adapted to Pi's actual APIs. The patch parser
uses Codex's documented marker grammar with stricter, unambiguous context matches.
See third_party/codex/SOURCE.json for upstream paths and checksums.

The core and delegated-agent instructions retain the current public Codex
GPT-6.1-Sol model instructions, with Pi protocol adaptations. These and the
current code-review rubric are pinned to Codex commit
c0cc9fc820f62e4dbdde68214dd6d792d6c8a7ee (2026-11-12).
No private session instructions are used. Original public source snapshots
are kept in the development tree; provenance, Apache-2.0 license and the
upstream NOTICE are retained in third_party/codex-current.

Terminal response formatting (ExecCommandToolOutput), captured-stream
head/tail buffering and output truncation are JavaScript ports of that same
2026-11-12 Codex commit. The terminal card adapts its raw-output preview to Pi.
Pi supplies the byte budget, stream callbacks and process control; cancellation
and timeout diagnostics remain explicit. No Rust runtime is bundled.

